          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c4_concretely_single_eighty_gigabyte_a1",
          "text": "Concretely, a single eighty-gigabyte A100 GPU can run inference on a thirty-billion-parameter model, yet standard Adam fine-tuning on the same hardware is limited to only a two-point-seven-billion-parameter model.",
